":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.6888731761222653,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.29727994396451085,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.05822,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":38.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Precision BioSciences, Inc., a clinical stage gene editing company, develops in vivo gene editing therapies for gene edits, including gene insertion, excision, and elimination in the United States. The company offers ARCUS, a genome editing platform for DNA genome insertion, removal, and repair. It also provides PBGENE-HBV for the treatment of chronic hepatitis B virus (HBV) to eliminate covalently closed circular DNA with direct cuts and edits, as well as to inactivate integrated HBV DNA with the goal of long-lasting reductions in hepatitis B surface antigen; and PBGENE-DMD (Excision) for the treatment of Duchenne muscular dystrophy. In addition, the company develops PBGENE-3243 for the treatment of m.3243 associated mitochondrial diseases; and iECURE-OTC (Insertion) for ornithine transcarbamylase deficiency. It has collaboration agreements with TG Cell Therapy, Inc. to develop, manufacture, and commercialize azercabtagene zapreleucel for autoimmune diseases and other indications; and iECURE, Inc., an ARCUS-mediated targeted gene insertion. Precision BioSciences, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Durham, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael  Amoroso | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 69 people. Revenue per employee of $497K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 44%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $148K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Precision BioSciences, Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $289M market cap on $34M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","The company is burning through $66M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +13.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -36.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 30% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +13.0% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-2.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 152% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"te